scheduler: keep successful relogins in the drain loop

Issue #4 relogin transition.

A valid daemon Login received on an already logged-in connection now has an
explicit result: KeepConnection after compiler-environment replacement,
busy-install reset, and any required protocol-24 ConfCS delivery;
CloseConnection on type or delivery failure.  The historical unconditional
false return made the drain loop stop serving a live connection for one turn.

The new focused fixture covers modern and legacy protocol paths, state update,
required reply ordering, failed reply delivery, and a null connection.  The
exact historical false-success mutant must fail at the drain-loop ownership
assertion.  The executor also runs all existing protocol-neutral issue-4 gates
and their negative controls before committing.
